From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:11:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/79] server: TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE_DEFAULT offers the
 built-in tool to every thinking chat that fits

Ports the compute default from the dsv41 release line (e5172c4a2, 75d774470,
012767b62, 8a6ce56a3) onto the compute lane stack:

- compute_lane.Config.default (PREFIX_DEFAULT=1, needs the lane);
- compute_turns.requestTools: a thinking chat with no stop strings, logprobs
  or structured output and max_tokens >= default_min_tokens gets the built-in
  python tool unasked; a client's own python function keeps the name; a
  client's copy of the built-in declares it once; tool_choice "none" keeps it;
- the default's own calls never reach the client: an unrun call ends the
  reply at length (ownCalls, Generation.lane_own);
- runtime.compute_executed counts the calls the sandbox ran.

Left for the runner port: the trust guide under the default (runner_guide,
guideAsked) and the runner's cells in the counter (runner_cells reads 0).
